The region bounded by $y=1-x^2$ and the $x$-axis is rotated about the $x$-axis. Find the exact volume.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[x=18mm,y=18mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\fill[fill={rgb,255:red,212;green,232;blue,255}] (-1,0) -- plot[domain=-1:1,samples=61,variable=\x] ({\x},{1-(\x)*(\x)}) -- cycle;
\draw[black,->] (-1.5,0)--(1.5,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,-0.6)--(0,1.5);
\draw[black,thick] plot[domain=-1.25:1.25,samples=61,variable=\x] ({\x},{1-(\x)*(\x)});
\path (1.5,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,1.5) node[above] {$y$} (0.85,1.2) node {$y=1-x^2$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

The regions bounded by $y=x^3-9x$ and the $x$-axis are rotated about the $x$-axis. Find the exact total volume.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=1.5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\fill[fill={rgb,255:red,212;green,232;blue,255}] (-3,0) -- plot[domain=-3:0,samples=61,variable=\x] ({\x},{(\x)*(\x)*(\x)-9*(\x)}) -- cycle;
\fill[fill={rgb,255:red,212;green,232;blue,255}] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:3,samples=61,variable=\x] ({\x},{(\x)*(\x)*(\x)-9*(\x)}) -- cycle;
\draw[black,->] (-3.8,0)--(3.8,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,-13)--(0,14);
\draw[black,thick] plot[domain=-3.4:3.4,samples=101,variable=\x] ({\x},{(\x)*(\x)*(\x)-9*(\x)});
\path (3.8,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,14) node[above] {$y$} (2.1,12) node {$y=x^3-9x$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
